model GetExecutorConfigResponseBody = {
  code?: int32(name='Code', description='The response code.', example='200'),
  data?: {
    config?: string(name='Config', description='The default global configuration content for the Data Integration synchronization Solutions node, which specifies the default processing policy for different DDL message types. Example:
{"RENAMECOLUMN":"WARNING","DROPTABLE":"WARNING","CREATETABLE":"WARNING","MODIFYCOLUMN":"WARNING","TRUNCATETABLE":"WARNING","DROPCOLUMN":"WARNING","ADDCOLUMN":"WARNING","RENAMETABLE":"WARNING"}

DDL message types:
- RENAMECOLUMN: Rename a column.
- DROPTABLE: Delete a table.
- CREATETABLE: Create a table.
- MODIFYCOLUMN: Modify a column type.
- TRUNCATETABLE: Truncate a table.
- DROPCOLUMN: Delete a column.
- ADDCOLUMN: Add a column.
- RENAMETABLE: Rename a table.

When DataWorks receives a DDL message of the corresponding type, the processing policy is as follows:
- WARNING: Discard the message directly and record alerting information in the real-time synchronization log, indicating that the message was discarded due to an execute error.
- IGNORE: Discard the message directly without sending it to the destination data source.
- CRITICAL: Set the real-time synchronization node to the error state and stop the node.
- NORMAL: Forward the message to the destination data source for processing. Because different destination data sources may have a different processing policy for DDL messages, DataWorks only forwards the message.', example='[{"cluster":"c2c619b5129e0400fa3df263b249622aa","namespace":"default","service":"xxljob-http-demo1-svc"}]'),
    executorType?: string(name='ExecutorType', description='The executor type.', example='k8s_service'),
  }(name='Data', description='The query result.'),
  message?: string(name='Message', description='The error message.', example='not support query script history, please upgrade engine version to 2.2.2+'),
  requestId?: string(name='RequestId', description='Id of the request', example='39938688-0BAB-5AD8-BF02-F4910FAC7589'),
  success?: boolean(name='Success', description='Indicates whether the request was successful.', example='true'),
}

